    "validation": "One shared four-byte status word per bound frame. Every thread verifies its source, coverage (when present) and final output. The host clears before submit and checks after the real GPU fence. No full-frame validation readback.",
    "apiContract": {
      "ingress": "Native caller attests extended-linear sRGB premultiplied top-left processed image, initialized backing and joined producer. Bind validates same MTLDevice identity and registryID, actual IOSurface plane, FourCC, bytes/pixel, row stride, allocation, sample count, usage, dimensions, and distinct storages. Empty mask on an unmasked plan binds its unused sample slot to the same input texture.",
      "ownership": "Call plan_open with CPU for portable validation, metal_program_open with native device, frame_bind with optional host lease. The frame retains program/device/native textures after original handles close. Caller serializes frame use and retains its own native presentation lease through final consumption.",
      "completion": "Join on a worker; post-submit cancellation or wgpu wait failure holds leases through the retained native command’s terminal status. The isolated real timeout used an unsignaled MTLSharedEvent then zero deadline, signaled the predecessor and drained. Publish requires current revision again on the app actor. GPU-rejected or stale output remains unpublished scratch.",
      "limits": "Selected RGBA32Float / R32Float IOSurfaces only, on one unified-memory Apple Metal device tested. A lazy CIImage without pre-existing compatible storage needs separate materialization accounting. A BGRA8 destination uses the existing ICC/display conversion. Physical device loss and multi-GPU selection have source checks but lack hardware-injection results."
